**Related Spec**: specs/597-delivery-pr-body-copies-verification-report-headings-into-the-verification-section-and-drops-the-changed-path-evidence/

# File: scripts/__tests__/delivery-pull-request-body-indented-headings.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/602-exclude-every-gate-recognized-heading-from-the-delivery-pr-body-s-verification-section/requirements.md
Feature: Exclude every gate-recognized heading from the delivery PR body's Verification section

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Indented heading lines are not copied
    Given a verification report with the line "### Results (`npm test` passed)" indented by <indent>
    When the delivery pull-request body is built
    Then the body does not contain that line
    And the only body line the gate's heading rule matches is "## Verification"

    Examples:
      | indent       |
      | four spaces  |
      | eight spaces |
      | one tab      |

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Changed paths stay verification evidence
    Given a verification report with a heading-shaped line indented by four spaces and changed paths "VERSION", "package.json" and ".claude-plugin/plugin.json"
    When the built body is evaluated by the contribution evidence check
    Then every changed path is matched and the evaluation passes

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Command results are still copied
    Given a verification report with the line <line>
    When the delivery pull-request body is built
    Then that line appears unchanged in the Verification section before "Changed paths:"

    Examples:
      | line                                   |
      | "- `npm test` — passed"                |
      | "\| `git diff --check` \| Pass \|"     |
      | "    - `npm test` — passed"            |
